# Root PACKAGE file: registers buck2's cfg-modifier machinery so that
# `buck2 build ... -m //buck2/constraints:opt` (or `:dev`) works (see
# buck2.md TODO "we should support different build modes"). This can only
# be done from the repository root PACKAGE file (set_cfg_constructor's own
# restriction) - there is nowhere else to put it.
#
# Unlike the rest of this cell's own buck2/*.bzl (byte-identical to
# Glean's own copies - see buck2.md's "make buck2/ and hsthrift/buck2/
# identical" entry), the logic here genuinely can't run unconditionally:
# when this checkout is nested inside another project (e.g. Glean), that
# project's own root PACKAGE file is the one and only one allowed to call
# set_cfg_constructor() project-wide - this cell's own copy of that exact
# same call, evaluated as `hsthrift//PACKAGE` rather than `root//PACKAGE`,
# hits that restriction and hard-errors the whole build (confirmed
# directly). Only when this checkout is itself the outermost project (its
# own `.buckconfig` maps `root = .`, so this file evaluates as
# `root//PACKAGE`) is the call actually allowed -
# cfg_constructor_if_standalone() checks that via get_cell_name().
#
# The condition itself has to live in buck2/cfg_constructor_if_standalone.
# bzl, not here - a PACKAGE file can only contain a flat sequence of
# top-level calls (no `if`/`def` directly in it, confirmed directly).
load("//buck2:cfg_constructor_if_standalone.bzl", "cfg_constructor_if_standalone", "dev_modifiers_if_standalone")
load("@prelude//cfg/modifier/set_cfg_modifiers.bzl", "set_cfg_modifiers")

cfg_constructor_if_standalone()

# set_cfg_modifiers() has to be called directly from here, not via a
# helper in cfg_constructor_if_standalone.bzl - see that file's own
# comment for why.
set_cfg_modifiers(
    cfg_modifiers = dev_modifiers_if_standalone(),
)
